#: MD.md:1
msgid "Molecular Dynamics Simulation"
msgstr "Molecular Dynamics シミュレーション"

#: MD.md:3
msgid ""
"Let's start with a Langevin simulation without bias. In LJ dimensionless "
"reduced units (assuming $\\epsilon$ = 1 eV, $\\sigma$ = 1 $\\textrm Å$ and m"
" = 1 a.m.u), the parameters of the simulation are $k_\\text{B}T=0.1$, "
"friction coefficient fixed equal to 1 and a time step of 0.005."
msgstr ""
"まず Bias なしの Langevin MD から始めます。LJ の無次元 Reduced Units（$\\epsilon$ = 1 "
"eV、$\\sigma$ = 1 $\\textrm Å$、m = 1 a.m.u）で、$k_\\text{B}T=0.1$、Friction "
"Coefficient は1、Time Step は0.005です。"

#: MD.md:8
msgid ""
"In principle, the system should explore all the configuration space due to "
"thermal fluctuations. However, we can see that the system remains in the "
"same conformational state, even when we simulate for a long time. This "
"happens because the system gets trapped in a local minimum and a complete "
"exploration of the configuration space is too expensive computationally. "
"Figure 2 -blue dots- shows the trajectory obtained from the following "
"unbiased Molecular Dynamics [`MD.py`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/MD.py):"
msgstr ""
"原理的には熱揺らぎで全 Configuration 空間を探索するはずですが、長時間でも同じ Conformation "
"に留まります。局所極小に捕まり、全探索のコストが高すぎるためです。図2の青点は、次の Unbiased MD "
"[`MD.py`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/MD.py) の Trajectory です。"

#: MD.md:48
msgid ""
"Where [`plumedLJ.dat`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/plumedLJ.dat) contains the next "
"information:"
msgstr ""
"[`plumedLJ.dat`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/plumedLJ.dat) は次の内容です。"

#: MD.md:58
msgid ""
"This simulation starts from the configuration of minimum energy, whose "
"coordinates are imported from "
"[`isomerLJ.xyz`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/isomer.xyz). As you can see in Figure 2, "
"the system remains around that state and it does not jump to the other "
"isomers, thereby not fully sampling all possible configurations of the "
"system. It is therefore necessary to use an enhanced sampling method. In "
"this tutorial, we implement Well-Tempered Metadynamics."
msgstr ""
"最小エネルギー構造 [`isomerLJ.xyz`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/isomer.xyz) から開始します。図2のように周囲に留まり、別の Isomer"
" に移らず、全 Configuration を Sampling できません。そこで Enhanced Sampling として Well-"
"Tempered Metadynamics を使います。"

#: MD.md:68
msgid "**WARNING**"
msgstr "**注意**"

#: MD.md:70
msgid ""
"Note that in the plumed setup, there is a line with the keyword `UNITS`, "
"which is necessary because all parameters and output files are assumed to be"
" in plumed internal units. This line is important to maintain the units of "
"all plumed parameters and outputs in ASE units. You can ignore this line if "
"you are aware of the unit conversion."
msgstr ""
"`UNITS` の行に注意してください。PLUMED のパラメータと出力は既定で内部単位なので、この行で ASE "
"単位に合わせます。単位変換を理解していれば省略できます。"

#: MD.md:73
msgid "Post Processing Analysis"
msgstr "後処理解析"

#: MD.md:75
msgid ""
"Once you have the trajectory of an MD simulation and you want to compute a "
"set of CVs of that trajectory, you can reconstruct the plumed files without "
"running again the simulation. As an example, let's use the trajectory "
"created in the last example to rewrite the COLVAR file with the code "
"[`postpro.py`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/postpro.py):"
msgstr ""
"既存 MD Trajectory の CV は、MD を再実行せず PLUMED 出力を再作成できます。先ほどの Trajectory から "
"[`postpro.py`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/postpro.py) で COLVAR を作り直します。"

#: MD.md:105
msgid ""
"This code, as well as the previous one, generates a file called COLVAR with "
"the value of the CVs. All PLUMED files begin with a header that describes "
"the fields that it contains. In this case, the header looks like:"
msgstr "前のコードと同様、CV を含む COLVAR を生成します。PLUMED 出力の先頭には列を説明する Header があり、今回は、"

#: MD.md:115
msgid ""
"As you can see, the first column corresponds to the time, the second one is "
"the second central moment (SCM) and the third column is the third central "
"moment (TCM). When we plot this trajectory in the space of these CVs (that "
"is, the second and third columns) we obtain this result:"
msgstr ""
"第1列は時間、第2列は Second Central Moment (SCM)、第3列は Third Central Moment (TCM) "
"です。第2・3列の CV 空間に描くと、"

#: MD.md:124
msgid ""
"**Figure 2.** Unbiased MD trajectory (blue dots) in the space of the "
"collective variables second and third central moment. Orange stars represent"
" the location of the local minima isomers of the LJ cluster in this space."
msgstr "**図2。** SCM・TCM 空間の Unbiased MD（青点）。橙の星は LJ Cluster の局所極小 Isomer です。"

#: MD.md:128
msgid ""
"Note that the system remains confined in the same stable state. Therefore, "
"the MD simulation is too short and it is not possible to explore all "
"configurations or to obtain a statistical study of the possible "
"configurations of the system. An alternative is to use an enhanced sampling "
"method. In this case, we implement Well-Tempered Metadynamics for "
"reconstructing the Free Energy Surface (FES)."
msgstr ""
"同じ安定状態に留まるため、この長さでは全 Configuration の探索や統計解析に不十分です。Well-Tempered Metadynamics"
" で自由エネルギー表面 (FES) を再構成します。"

